{
  "description": "Declaring a name `global` NAMES the root scope's binding of that name, whether or not one already exists (spec/execution-model.md:576-583): `:count = 5` then `global count = 0` leaves one binding, now shared and holding `0`, and a second `global count = 2` assigns again rather than creating a second binding or raising `ol-duplicate-definition`. A `global` declaration registers no callable, so it is not a declaration in the sense spec/grammar.md gives that word.",
